\s1 Nehemiah’s Prayer
\p \v 1 \w These are the words|strong="H01697"\w* \w of Nehemiah|strong="H05166"\w* \w son|strong="H01121"\w* \w of Hacaliah|strong="H02446"\w*:
\p \w In the month|strong="H02320"\w* \w of Chislev|strong="H03691"\w*,\f + \fr 1:1 \fqa Chislev \ft is the ninth month of the Hebrew lunar calendar, usually occurring within the months of November and December.\f* \w in the twentieth|strong="H06242"\w* \w year|strong="H08141"\w*, \w while I|strong="H00589"\w* \w was|strong="H01961"\w* \w in the citadel|strong="H01002"\w* \w of Susa|strong="H07800"\w*, \v 2 \w Hanani|strong="H02607"\w*, \w one|strong="H00259"\w* \w of my brothers|strong="H00251"\w*, \w arrived|strong="H00935"\w* \w with men|strong="H00582"\w* \w from Judah|strong="H03063"\w*. \w So I questioned them|strong="H07592"\w* \w about|strong="H05921"\w* \w the remnant|strong="H06413"\w* \w of the Jews|strong="H03064"\w* \w who|strong="H00834"\w* \w had survived|strong="H07604"\w* \w the exile|strong="H07628"\w*, \w and also about|strong="H05921"\w* \w Jerusalem|strong="H03389"\w*.
\p \v 3 \w And they told|strong="H00559"\w* me, “\w The remnant|strong="H07604"\w* \w who|strong="H00834"\w* \w survived|strong="H07604"\w* \w the exile|strong="H07628"\w* \w are there|strong="H08033"\w* \w in the province|strong="H04082"\w*, \w in great|strong="H01419"\w* \w trouble|strong="H07451"\w* \w and disgrace|strong="H02781"\w*. \w The wall|strong="H02346"\w* \w of Jerusalem|strong="H03389"\w* \w is broken down|strong="H06555"\w*, \w and its gates|strong="H08179"\w* \w have been burned|strong="H03341"\w* \w with fire|strong="H00784"\w*.”
\p \v 4 \w When I heard|strong="H08085"\w* \w these|strong="H00428"\w* \w words|strong="H01697"\w*, \w I sat down|strong="H03427"\w* \w and wept|strong="H01058"\w*. \w I mourned|strong="H00056"\w* \w for days|strong="H03117"\w*, \w fasting|strong="H06684"\w* \w and praying|strong="H06419"\w* \w before|strong="H06440"\w* \w the God|strong="H00430"\w* \w of heaven|strong="H08064"\w*.
\p \v 5 \w Then I said|strong="H00559"\w*:
\p “\w O|strong="H00577"\w* \w LORD|strong="H03068"\w*, \w God|strong="H00430"\w* \w of heaven|strong="H08064"\w*, \w the great|strong="H01419"\w* \w and awesome|strong="H03372"\w* \w God|strong="H00410"\w* \w who keeps|strong="H08104"\w* \w His covenant|strong="H01285"\w* \w of loving devotion|strong="H02617"\w*\f + \fr 1:5 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa chesed \ft are translated here and in most cases throughout the Scriptures as \fqa loving devotion\ft ; the range of meaning includes \fqa love\ft , \fqa goodness\ft , \fqa kindness\ft , \fqa faithfulness\ft , and \fqa mercy\ft , as well as \fqa loyalty to a covenant\ft .\f* \w with those who love Him|strong="H00157"\w* \w and keep|strong="H08104"\w* \w His commandments|strong="H04687"\w*, \v 6 \w let Your eyes|strong="H05869"\w* \w be|strong="H01961"\w* \w open|strong="H06605"\w* \w and Your ears|strong="H00241"\w* \w attentive|strong="H07183"\w* \w to hear|strong="H08085"\w* \w the prayer|strong="H08605"\w* \w that|strong="H00834"\w* \w I|strong="H00595"\w*, \w Your servant|strong="H05650"\w*, \w now|strong="H03117"\w* \w pray|strong="H06419"\w* \w before You|strong="H06440"\w* \w day|strong="H03119"\w* \w and night|strong="H03915"\w* \w for|strong="H05921"\w* \w Your servants|strong="H05650"\w*, \w the Israelites|strong="H01121"\w*.
\p \w I confess|strong="H03034"\w* \w the sins|strong="H02403"\w* \w that|strong="H00834"\w* \w we Israelites|strong="H01121"\w* \w have committed|strong="H02398"\w* against You. \w Both I|strong="H00589"\w* \w and my father’s|strong="H00001"\w* \w house|strong="H01004"\w* \w have sinned|strong="H02398"\w*. \v 7 \w We have behaved corruptly|strong="H02254"\w* against You \w and have not|strong="H03808"\w* \w kept|strong="H08104"\w* \w the commandments|strong="H04687"\w*, \w statutes|strong="H02706"\w*, \w and ordinances|strong="H04941"\w* \w that|strong="H00834"\w* \w You gave|strong="H06680"\w* \w Your servant|strong="H05650"\w* \w Moses|strong="H04872"\w*.
\p \v 8 \w Remember|strong="H02142"\w*, \w I pray|strong="H04994"\w*, \w the word|strong="H01697"\w* \w that|strong="H00834"\w* \w You commanded|strong="H06680"\w* \w Your servant|strong="H05650"\w* \w Moses|strong="H04872"\w* \w when You said|strong="H00559"\w*, ‘\w If you|strong="H00859"\w* \w are unfaithful|strong="H04603"\w*, \w I|strong="H00589"\w* \w will scatter|strong="H06327"\w* \w you|strong="H00853"\w* \w among the nations|strong="H05971"\w*, \v 9 \w but if you return|strong="H07725"\w* \w to Me|strong="H00413"\w* \w and keep|strong="H08104"\w* \w and practice|strong="H06213"\w* \w My commandments|strong="H04687"\w*, \w then even if|strong="H00518"\w* \w your exiles|strong="H05080"\w* \w have been|strong="H01961"\w* \w banished to the farthest|strong="H07097"\w* \w horizon|strong="H08064"\w*,\f + \fr 1:9 \ft Or \fqa to the extremity of the heavens\f* \w I will gather them|strong="H06908"\w* \w from there|strong="H08033"\w* \w and bring them|strong="H00935"\w* \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w the place|strong="H04725"\w* \w I have chosen|strong="H00977"\w* \w as a dwelling|strong="H07931"\w* \w for|strong="H00853"\w* \w My Name|strong="H08034"\w*.’\f + \fr 1:9 \ft Deuteronomy 30:1–4\f*
\p \v 10 \w They|strong="H01992"\w* \w are Your servants|strong="H05650"\w* \w and Your people|strong="H05971"\w*. \w You redeemed|strong="H06299"\w* \w them|strong="H00834"\w* \w by Your great|strong="H01419"\w* \w power|strong="H03581"\w* \w and mighty|strong="H02389"\w* \w hand|strong="H03027"\w*. \v 11 \w O Lord|strong="H00136"\w*, \w may Your ear|strong="H00241"\w* \w be|strong="H01961"\w* \w attentive|strong="H07183"\w* \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w my prayer|strong="H08605"\w* \w and to|strong="H00413"\w* \w the prayers|strong="H08605"\w* \w of Your servants|strong="H05650"\w*\f + \fr 1:11 \ft Literally \fqa to the prayer of Your servant and to the prayer of Your servants\f* \w who delight|strong="H02655"\w* \w to revere|strong="H03372"\w* \w Your name|strong="H08034"\w*. \w Give Your servant|strong="H05650"\w* \w success|strong="H06743"\w* \w this day|strong="H03117"\w*, \w I pray|strong="H04994"\w*, \w and grant him|strong="H05414"\w* \w mercy|strong="H07356"\w* \w in the sight|strong="H06440"\w* \w of this|strong="H02088"\w* \w man|strong="H00376"\w*.”
\p (\w At that time I|strong="H00589"\w* \w was|strong="H01961"\w* \w the cupbearer|strong="H04945"\w* \w to the king|strong="H04428"\w*.)
\c 2
\s1 Nehemiah Sent to Jerusalem
\p \v 1 \w Now|strong="H01961"\w* \w in the month|strong="H02320"\w* \w of Nisan|strong="H05212"\w*,\f + \fr 2:1 \fqa Nisan \ft is the first month of the Hebrew lunar calendar, usually occurring within the months of March and April.\f* \w in the twentieth|strong="H06242"\w* \w year|strong="H08141"\w* \w of King|strong="H04428"\w* \w Artaxerxes|strong="H00783"\w*, \w when wine|strong="H03196"\w* \w was set before him|strong="H06440"\w*, \w I took|strong="H05375"\w* \w the wine|strong="H03196"\w* \w and gave|strong="H05414"\w* \w it to the king|strong="H04428"\w*. \w I had never|strong="H03808"\w* \w been|strong="H01961"\w* \w sad|strong="H07451"\w* \w in his presence|strong="H06440"\w*, \v 2 \w so the king|strong="H04428"\w* \w said|strong="H00559"\w* to me, “\w Why is|strong="H04069"\w* \w your face|strong="H06440"\w* \w sad|strong="H07451"\w*, \w though you are|strong="H00859"\w* \w not|strong="H00369"\w* \w ill|strong="H02470"\w*? \w This|strong="H02088"\w* \w could only be|strong="H00369"\w* \w sadness|strong="H07455"\w* \w of the heart|strong="H03820"\w*.”
\p \w I was overwhelmed with fear|strong="H03372"\w* \v 3 \w and replied|strong="H00559"\w* \w to the king|strong="H04428"\w*, “\w May the king|strong="H04428"\w* \w live forever|strong="H02421"\w*! \w Why|strong="H04069"\w* \w should I not|strong="H03808"\w* \w be sad|strong="H07489"\w* \w when|strong="H00834"\w* \w the city|strong="H05892"\w* \w where|strong="H01004"\w* \w my fathers|strong="H00001"\w* \w are buried|strong="H06913"\w* \w lies in ruins|strong="H02720"\w*, \w and its gates|strong="H08179"\w* \w have been destroyed|strong="H00398"\w* \w by fire|strong="H00784"\w*?”
\p \v 4 “\w What|strong="H04100"\w* \w is your|strong="H00859"\w* \w request|strong="H01245"\w*?” \w replied|strong="H00559"\w* \w the king|strong="H04428"\w*.
\p \w So I prayed|strong="H06419"\w* \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w the God|strong="H00430"\w* \w of heaven|strong="H08064"\w* \v 5 \w and answered|strong="H00559"\w* \w the king|strong="H04428"\w*, “\w If|strong="H00518"\w* \w it pleases|strong="H02896"\w* \w the king|strong="H04428"\w*, \w and if|strong="H00518"\w* \w your servant|strong="H05650"\w* \w has found favor|strong="H03190"\w* \w in your sight|strong="H06440"\w*, \w I ask that|strong="H00834"\w* \w you send me|strong="H07971"\w* \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w Judah|strong="H03063"\w*, \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w the city|strong="H05892"\w* \w where my fathers|strong="H00001"\w* \w are buried|strong="H06913"\w*, \w so that I may rebuild it|strong="H01129"\w*.”
\p \v 6 \w Then the king|strong="H04428"\w*, \w with the queen|strong="H07694"\w* \w seated|strong="H03427"\w* \w beside him|strong="H00681"\w*, \w asked|strong="H00559"\w* me, “\w How long|strong="H05704"\w* \w will your journey|strong="H04109"\w* \w take|strong="H01961"\w*, \w and when|strong="H04970"\w* \w will you return|strong="H07725"\w*?” \w So it pleased|strong="H03190"\w* \w the king|strong="H04428"\w* \w to send me|strong="H07971"\w*, \w and I set|strong="H05414"\w* \w a time|strong="H02165"\w*.
\p \v 7 \w I also said|strong="H00559"\w* \w to him|strong="H04428"\w*, “\w If|strong="H00518"\w* \w it pleases|strong="H02896"\w* \w the king|strong="H04428"\w*, \w may letters|strong="H00107"\w* \w be given|strong="H05414"\w* to me \w for|strong="H05921"\w* \w the governors|strong="H06346"\w* \w west|strong="H05676"\w* \w of the Euphrates|strong="H05104"\w*,\f + \fr 2:7 \ft Hebrew \fqa beyond the River\ft ; also in verse 9\f* \w so that|strong="H00834"\w* \w they will grant me safe passage|strong="H05674"\w* \w until|strong="H05704"\w* \w I reach|strong="H00935"\w* \w Judah|strong="H03063"\w*. \v 8 \w And may I have a letter|strong="H00107"\w* \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w Asaph|strong="H00623"\w*, \w keeper|strong="H08104"\w* \w of the king’s|strong="H00834"\w* \w forest|strong="H06508"\w*, \w so that|strong="H00834"\w* \w he will give|strong="H05414"\w* me \w timber|strong="H06086"\w* \w to make beams|strong="H07136"\w* \w for|strong="H00853"\w* \w the gates|strong="H08179"\w* \w of the citadel|strong="H01002"\w* \w to the temple|strong="H01004"\w*, \w for the city|strong="H05892"\w* \w wall|strong="H02346"\w*, \w and for the house|strong="H01004"\w* \w I will occupy|strong="H00935"\w*.”
\p \w And because the gracious|strong="H02896"\w* \w hand|strong="H03027"\w* \w of my God|strong="H00430"\w* \w was upon me|strong="H05921"\w*, \w the king|strong="H04428"\w* \w granted|strong="H05414"\w* my requests.
\p \v 9 \w Then I went|strong="H00935"\w* \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w the governors|strong="H06346"\w* \w west|strong="H05676"\w* \w of the Euphrates|strong="H05104"\w* \w and gave|strong="H05414"\w* them \w the king’s|strong="H04428"\w* \w letters|strong="H00107"\w*. \w The king|strong="H04428"\w* \w had also sent|strong="H07971"\w* \w army|strong="H02428"\w* \w officers|strong="H08269"\w* \w and cavalry|strong="H06571"\w* \w with me|strong="H05973"\w*.
