\s1 Nehemiah Inspects the Walls
\p \v 11 \w After I had arrived|strong="H00935"\w* \w in|strong="H00413"\w* \w Jerusalem|strong="H03389"\w* \w and had been|strong="H01961"\w* \w there|strong="H08033"\w* \w three|strong="H07969"\w* \w days|strong="H03117"\w*, \v 12 \w I|strong="H00589"\w* \w set out|strong="H06965"\w* \w at night|strong="H03915"\w* \w with|strong="H05973"\w* \w a few|strong="H04592"\w* \w men|strong="H00582"\w*. \w I did not|strong="H03808"\w* \w tell|strong="H05046"\w* \w anyone|strong="H00120"\w* \w what|strong="H04100"\w* \w my God|strong="H00430"\w* \w had laid|strong="H05414"\w* \w on|strong="H00413"\w* \w my heart|strong="H03820"\w* \w to do|strong="H06213"\w* \w for Jerusalem|strong="H03389"\w*. \w The only|strong="H03588"\w* \w animal|strong="H00929"\w* \w with me|strong="H05973"\w* \w was the one|strong="H00929"\w* \w on which|strong="H00834"\w* \w I|strong="H00589"\w* \w was riding|strong="H07392"\w*.
\p \v 13 \w So I went out|strong="H03318"\w* \w at night|strong="H03915"\w* \w through the Valley|strong="H01516"\w* \w Gate|strong="H08179"\w* \w toward|strong="H00413"\w* \w the Well|strong="H05869"\w* \w of the Serpent|strong="H08577"\w*\f + \fr 2:13 \ft Or \fqa Dragon \ft or \fqa Jackal\f* \w and the Dung|strong="H00830"\w* \w Gate|strong="H08179"\w*, \w and I inspected|strong="H07663"\w* \w the walls|strong="H02346"\w* \w of Jerusalem|strong="H03389"\w* \w that|strong="H00834"\w* \w had been broken down|strong="H06555"\w* \w and the gates|strong="H08179"\w* \w that had been destroyed|strong="H00398"\w* \w by fire|strong="H00784"\w*.
\p \v 14 \w Then I went on|strong="H05674"\w* \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w the Fountain|strong="H05869"\w* \w Gate|strong="H08179"\w* \w and the King’s|strong="H04428"\w* \w Pool|strong="H01295"\w*, \w but there was no|strong="H00369"\w* \w room|strong="H04725"\w* \w for the animal|strong="H00929"\w* \w under me|strong="H08478"\w* \w to get through|strong="H05674"\w*; \v 15 \w so I|strong="H01961"\w* \w went up|strong="H05927"\w* \w the valley|strong="H05158"\w* \w by night|strong="H03915"\w* \w and|strong="H01961"\w* \w inspected|strong="H07663"\w* \w the wall|strong="H02346"\w*. \w Then I headed back|strong="H07725"\w* \w and reentered|strong="H00935"\w* \w through the Valley|strong="H01516"\w* \w Gate|strong="H08179"\w*.
\p \v 16 \w The officials|strong="H05461"\w* \w did not|strong="H03808"\w* \w know|strong="H03045"\w* \w where|strong="H00575"\w* \w I had gone|strong="H01980"\w* \w or what|strong="H04100"\w* \w I|strong="H00589"\w* \w was doing|strong="H06213"\w*, \w for I had not|strong="H03808"\w* \w yet|strong="H05704"\w* \w told|strong="H05046"\w* \w the Jews|strong="H03064"\w* \w or priests|strong="H03548"\w* \w or nobles|strong="H02715"\w* \w or officials|strong="H05461"\w* \w or any other|strong="H03499"\w* \w workers|strong="H04399"\w*. \v 17 \w Then I said|strong="H00559"\w* \w to them|strong="H00413"\w*, “\w You|strong="H00859"\w* \w see|strong="H07200"\w* \w the trouble|strong="H07451"\w* \w we are|strong="H00587"\w* in. \w Jerusalem|strong="H03389"\w* \w lies in ruins|strong="H02720"\w*, \w and its gates|strong="H08179"\w* \w have been burned down|strong="H03341"\w*. \w Come|strong="H01980"\w*, \w let us rebuild|strong="H01129"\w* \w the wall|strong="H02346"\w* \w of Jerusalem|strong="H03389"\w*, \w so that we will no|strong="H03808"\w* \w longer|strong="H05750"\w* \w be|strong="H01961"\w* \w a disgrace|strong="H02781"\w*.”
